<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.cron-google-tasks</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>curl -sS -m 850 -H "Authorization: Bearer $(grep '^CRON_SECRET=' __APP_DIR__/.env.local | cut -d= -f2-)" http://localhost:3000/api/cron/google-tasks</string>
  </array>
  <!-- Every 4 hours, all day (Richard, 2026-09-15: a to-do list does not need
       quarter-hourly polling). Note what this does NOT slow down: anything
       ticked off inside the platform still reaches Google in seconds via
       queueTaskPush. This interval only bounds the other direction — how long a
       task completed on a phone, or created in bulk by a confirm route, waits
       before the board catches up.

       If you change it, change STALE_AFTER_HOURS in src/lib/system-health.ts to
       match, or the health card reports a healthy sync as stalled.

       StartInterval rather than the
       StartCalendarInterval every other job here uses, because those are all
       daily or weekly and this one is not.

       Minutes, not nightly: three confirm routes (meeting intake, email
       ingestion, action items) create tasks in bulk without going through
       /api/tasks, so they never fire the immediate push. "The tasks someone
       assigned you this morning turn up tomorrow" is the wrong answer for a
       to-do list, and it is the reason those routes were left out of the
       immediate path rather than made to pay twenty Google round trips inside
       a human-facing click.

       ThrottleInterval matches, so a run that overruns cannot stack. -->
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>14400</integer>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>14400</integer>
  <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
  <false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-google-tasks.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-google-tasks.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
